          "r20"
        ]
      },
      {
        "finding": "At a constant 1.2B parameters, going from L=16 to L=32 naively lowers average ARC-C/HellaSwag accuracy by 0.5. Adding sparsity mechanisms raises it to 44.1 (Figure 1, Section 5).",
        "proposed_claim": "At fixed parameter count, depth/width shape affects downstream accuracy, depending on sparsity mechanisms (a downstream analogue of V4, not loss).",
        "row_ids": []
      }
    ],
    "controls": "y",
